{
  "title": "Total Ankle Arthroplasty",
  "url": "https://www.orthobullets.com/foot-and-ankle/12133/total-ankle-arthroplasty",
  "subtitle": "Updated: Aug 18 2026",
  "sections": [
    {
      "text": "summary",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Total Ankle Arthroplasty is an alternative to ankle arthrodesis for the treatment of end-stage ankle osteoarthritis.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "The procedure attempts to preserve functional range of motion, which would otherwise be sacrificed with ankle arthrodesis.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Contraindications include active infection, peripheral vascular disease, charcot arthropathy, severe osteoporosis, osteonecrosis of the talus, and peripheral neuropathy.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "History",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "History",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "first generation TAA",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "majority of designs were highly constrained, or semi-constrained two component prostheses",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "used cement fixation on both the talar and tibial sides",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "**high incidence of loosening**, wide osteolysis, subsidence, and mechanical failure of prosthesis components",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "second generation TAA",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "majority are two-component fixed-bearing systems with a **polyethylene bearing surface** incorporated into the talar or tibial component",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "more conservative bone cuts",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "elimination of bone cement in favour of **press-fit designs** with porous coating for bony ingrowth",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "third generation TAA",
              "table": null,
              "images": [
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/12133/images/taaex.jpg",
                  "caption": ""
                }
              ],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "characterized by the addition of a third component, **an independent polyethylene mobile-bearing meniscus**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "place a greater importance on the use of ligaments to retain stability, the need for anatomic balancing following component insertion, and minimal bone resection.",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Implants approved by the FDA",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Scandinavian Total Ankle Replacement (STAR; Small Bone Innovations, Morrisville, PA)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "INBONE (Wright Medical Technology, Arlington, TN)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "Agility (DePuy, Warsaw, IN)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "Salto Talaris (Tornier, Montbonnot, France)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Outcomes",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "pain and function",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "significant improvement in pain and function",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "pre-operative ROM best predictor for post-operative ROM with minimal additional benefit in ROM gained from TAA",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "little high quality evidence comparing TAA vs. ankle arthrodesis",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "TAA with superior performance on uneven surfaces compared to ankle arthrodesis",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "survivorship",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "TAA survivorship at 10 years ranges from 70% to 90%",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": ">80% survivorship in patients <50 years of age at 5 years",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "no evidence that three component designs are better than two component designs",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Indications",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Indications",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "diagnosis",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**unilateral or bilateral end-stage ankle OA**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "favorable patient factors",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "older (middle- to old-aged), low demand, reasonably mobile patient with no significant co-morbidities",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "normal or low body mass index",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "well-aligned and stable hindfoot",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "good soft tissues conditions",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Contraindications",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "active infection",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "**peripheral vascular disease**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "inadequate soft-tissue envelope",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "Charcot arthropathy",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "insufficient bone stock",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "severe osteoporosis",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "**osteonecrosis of the talus**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "**peripheral neuropathy**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Preoperative Imaging",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Radiographs",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "recommended views",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "weight-bearing AP and lateral views of the ankle",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [
                    {
                      "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/12133/images/apankoa.jpg",
                      "caption": ""
                    },
                    {
                      "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/12133/images/latankoa.jpg",
                      "caption": ""
                    }
                  ],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "findings",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "extent of arthritis",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "MRI",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "findings",
              "table": null,
              "images": [
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/12133/images/avntalus.jpg",
                  "caption": ""
                }
              ],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "presence of osteonecrosis, amount of involvement, bone loss,and size of subchondral cysts",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Surgical Technique",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Approach",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "vast majority of systems utilize an **anterior approach** to the ankle, via the interval between tibialis anterior and extensor hallucis longus",
              "table": null,
              "images": [
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/12133/images/taaintraop.jpg",
                  "caption": ""
                }
              ],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Goals",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "to restore mechanical alignment to the ankle",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "achieved by alignment guides that allow for precise cuts of the tibia, talus, and in some systems the fibula",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "recent iterations of TAA systems have incorporated ligamentous balancing as a crucial part of the operative procedure",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "imperative to achieve a stable, neutrally aligned, plantigrade, weight-bearing position of the ankle and hindfoot",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "ligament reconstruction, tendon transfers, osteotomies, heel cord lengthening and arthrodesis may be necessary",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Technical Considerations",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "soft tissue considerations",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "use a long incision to decrease the tension on the skin",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "perform thick skin flaps to maintain vascularity",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "minimize use of retractors has been emphasized in the literature",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "avoid the tibialis anterior sheath",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "prevents tendon bowstringing and its resultant wound complications",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "implant placement",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "common technical errors include",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "placing the prosthesis too lateral",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "using too small a prosthesis, which subsides",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "failing to solve preoperative varus or valgus malalignment and attempting to replace an ankle that is too anteriorly subluxated",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Complications",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "**Delayed wound healing**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "most common",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "reported in 4% to 17% of cases in the literature",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**Superficial wound infection**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "**Deep wound infection**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "ranges from 0.5% to 3.5% of cases",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "prosthetic joint infection treated with explantation, antibiotics, and either reimplantation or salvage arthrodesis",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "studies have shown a low success rate of component reimplantation",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "painful TAA work-up should include CBC, ESR, and CRP",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**Sensory deficits**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "secondary to anterior incision and its proximity to the superficial and deep peroneal nerves",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "reported rates are as high as 21%",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**Intraoperative Fracture**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "medial > lateral malleolus",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "occur in the narrow bone bridge between the ankle joint and the outer cortex of the tibia or fibula",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "causes",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "overextending the plafond cut too medially or laterally",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "making a cut too proximal in the tibia",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "using an over-sized tibial component",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "distraction of the ankle with an external fixator",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "prevention",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "prophylactic K-wire pinning (or screw fixation) prior to osteotomy cut",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [
                    {
                      "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/12133/images/illus_c.jpg",
                      "caption": "Prophylactic pinning medial malleolus"
                    }
                  ],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**Component loosening**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "talar component fails more commonly than the tibial component",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**Subsidence**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "5",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "may need to convert to ankle fusion",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "decide if there is infection",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "decide whether to fuse across subtalar joint (TTC fusion)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "decide what bone graft to use",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "particulate cancellous graft (<2cm talar bone loss)",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "bulk allograft (>2cm bone loss)",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "femoral head allograft",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "2",
                          "children": [
                            {
                              "text": "graft of choice if TTC fusion is chosen",
                              "table": null,
                              "images": [],
                              "importance": "2",
                              "children": []
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "text": "Cambell allograft graft (wedges of tricortical iliac crest)",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "2",
                          "children": []
                        },
                        {
                          "text": "fresh-frozen distal tibial allograft",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "2",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "decide what type of fixation",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "nail",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "plate",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "nail and plate",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**Osteolysis**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "polyethylene wear results in osteolysis, with large, expansive cystic lesions in the tibia or talus",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "CT with metal artifact reduction protocol is the best study to evaluate for extent of osteolysis",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
